; Internet play (ONLINE) goes through Epic Online Services. The game reads
; eos.ini beside its executable; without it, ONLINE works on the local
; network only. The release ships the project's own eos.ini when it has one.
;
; To use your own product: create one at https://dev.epicgames.com/portal,
; add a client with the "Peer2Peer" policy, then fill in its five values and
; save this file as eos.ini next to the game (umk3-game on Linux, umk3-game64.exe on Windows).
; 64-bit builds only: the SDK has no 32-bit library.

[eos]
product=
sandbox=
deployment=
client_id=
client_secret=
